The question "which are MUST and which are SHOULD" is about whether a rule may be overridden. A MUST may not be overridden; a SHOULD may, with reason. That's actually a better reading of the level definitions: MUST = a gate (no override, no proceed); SHOULD = default (override allowed with reason). Then the test is: can a writer ever have a legitimate reason to do otherwise? If not → MUST. If yes → SHOULD. Enforcement is a separate question (the gate exists or must be built).

